// mitra-rust as Mitra sees it. Start here.
//
// mitra-rust is what Mitra knows of Rust: it reads the report of
// `cargo test`, finds
// the tie comments of Rust files and compares the code under them with
// the model. What it finds is brought as evidence.
//
//   code.mitra     the boundary: the Rust files and where they come from
//   reader.mitra   the contract `Reader` of mitra-lang, filled for Rust:
//                  the report of `cargo test`, the tied tests, the ties
//   source.mitra   finding tie comments in a Rust file
//   points.mitra   the single calls the unit tests pin
//
// A comment `// mitra: implements reader::Rust::tie` above a `fn` ties it to
// a function here, and `mitra tie` checks that the two agree.
